===Etymology 2===
{{wikidata lexeme|L327386}}
{{ety|en|id=big seat|:inh|enm:see<id:seat>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|se}}, {{m|enm|see|id=seat}}, from {{der|en|fro|see,sié||seat, throne; town, capital; episcopal see}}, from {{der|en|la|sēdēs||seat}}, referring to the bishop's [[throne]] or chair (compare ''seat of power'') in the [[cathedral]]; related to the Latin verb {{m|la|sedēre||to sit}}. {{doublet|en|sedes}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q665487 or Q2072238}} {{lb|en|Christianity}} A [[diocese#English:_Q665487|diocese]] or [[archdiocese#English:_Q2072238|archdiocese]]: a region of a church, generally headed by a [[bishop]] or an [[archbishop]].
#: {{hypo|en|bishopric<id:Q665487>|archbishopric<id:Q2072238>}}
# {{senseid|en|office of bishop or archbishop}} {{lb|en|Christianity}} The [[office]] of a bishop or archbishop.
#: {{hypo|en|bishopric<id:office of bishop>|archbishopric<id:office of archbishop>}}
#: {{cot|en|apse<id:chair of a bishop><qq:their chair or throne>}}
# {{senseid|en|seat of power}} A [[seat]]; a [[site]]; a place where [[sovereign]], [[autonomous]], or [[autocephalous]] power is [[exercise]]d.
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|year=1590|book=III|canto=VI|stanza=2|page=478|passage=Ioue laught on Venus from his ſouerayne '''ſee'''}}

